# Allowlist for scripts/check-no-local-paths.sh
#
# One entry per line:   <path-glob>[|<extended-regex>]
#   * <path-glob>   matches the repo-relative file path (bash pattern; `*` also matches `/`).
#   * <regex>       optional; when present the entry only covers lines matching it.
# Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are ignored. Keep entries as narrow as possible
# and say why the match is legitimate. Never allowlist a real credential - remove it.

# Repo-health checker defines the very patterns that detect machine-local paths.
scripts/check-repo-health.sh|/Users/|\.venv/bin/python

# TEMPORARY: split-audit document quotes the leaks it describes. Remove this entry once
# the document is scrubbed of the literal paths (re-sweep pending, see the hygiene note).
docs/design/repository-layout.md

# This note describes the patterns the guard rejects.
.agents/notes/implemented/process/*-open-source-hygiene.md

# Test data for the Windows path parser (`_parseFileInfo`); not a real user path.
tests/test_protocol/test_filesystem.test.ts|C:\\\\Users\\\\(test|docs)\\\\

# Deliberately invalid API key (one repeated character) used by the wrong-key E2E scenarios.
e2e/scenarios/10-cloud-readonly.mjs|e2b_(.)\1{19,}
# /home/sandbox is the sandbox-side home directory used as test data, not a developer path.
tests/test_cli/test_sandbox_system_extra_commands.test.ts|/home/sandbox
# Redaction regex for the config.toml warning text in the differential harness.
parity/diff/config_cmds.mjs|home\\/\\.ebx
